        <body>
            <div xml:id="d214-a6">

                <pb facs="0512" n="388" xml:id="pg388"/>

                <head>VI.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Office of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-05-28"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 28,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>A communication having been made to the honorable Senate of the Union that the
                    executive power, without declining to appreciate as patriotic and well
                    intentioned the conduct of our minister in Washington, has declared the bases of
                    the protocol of the 17th February to be inacceptable in a general point of view,
                    and in consequence has given to the negotiations the turn corresponding to such
                    ecision.</p>
                <p>This resolution ends for the present the important business to which the
                    documents published this day refer.</p>
                <p>The Secretary:</p>
                <closer><signed>BECERRA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
